1. e4 e5 2. f4 exf4 3. Bc4 Qh4+ 4. Kf1 b5 5. Bxb5 Nf6 6. Nf3 Qh6 7. d3 Nh5 8. Nh4 Qg5 9. Nf5 c6 10. g4 Nf6 11. Rg1 cxb5 12. h4 Qg6 13. h5 Qg5 14. Qf3 { Threatening to win the Queen by 15.xf4, as well as 15e5 attacking the Rook with his Queen while his King Pawn bites at the Knight. } 14... Ng8 { "One can not always be happy" says Nimzovich. } 15. Bxf4 Qf6 16. Nc3 Bc5 17. Nd5! Qxb2 18. Bd6! { "Ganz grossartig gespielt" says Gottschall. } 18... Bxg1 (18... Qxa1+ 19. Ke2 Qxg1 20. Nxg7+ Kd8 21. Bc7#) (18... Bxd6 19. Nxd6+ Kd8 20. Nxf7+ Ke8 21. Nd6+ Kd8 22. Qf8#) 19. e5! { "Have another Rook!" } 19... Qxa1+ 20. Ke2 Na6 21. Nxg7+ Kd8 22. Qf6+! Nxf6 23. Be7#! { White has given up Queen, two Rooks and a Biship for one single, miserable Pawn (and mate, the cynic might point out). } 1-0


