1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bc4 Bc5 4. b4 Bxb4 5. c3 Ba5 6. d4 exd4 7. O-O d3 8. Qb3 Qf6 9. e5 Qg6 (9... Nxe5 { White wins by } 10. Re1 (10. Nxe5) 10... d6 11. Qb5+) 10. Re1 Nge7 11. Ba3 b5 12. Qxb5 Rb8 13. Qa4 Bb6 { He cannot Castle into safety, as 14.xe7 would win a piece for White. } 14. Nbd2 Bb7 15. Ne4 Qf5 16. Bxd3 Qh5 { Running away from the threat of 17.f6+ winning the Queen. } 17. Nf6+! gxf6 18. exf6 Rg8 { Now comes what Lasker (who knows a good move when he sees one) says is "one of the most subtle and profound moves on record." } 19. Rad1! Qxf3 20. Rxe7+! Nxe7 21. Qxd7+! { And if this is not a million-dollar move, what is? } 21... Kxd7 22. Bf5+ Ke8 (22... Kc6 23. Bd7#) 23. Bd7+ Kd8 24. Bxe7# { 1-0 White wins. } 1-0


